                <pb facs="0192" n="1026" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1026"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/971a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-30T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1072. [From War Trade Board] for Chadbourne, No. 41, and repeat consuls:</p>
                <p>Before recommending changes enemy trading list confer British, French, Italian
                    colleagues. If agreement results report in duplicate simultaneously to State
                    Department and to Captain Stickney, United States Embassy, Paris. If
                    disagreement results, send your opinion and variant opinions of colleagues with
                    reasons. In each case give nationality and residence of person or association
                    recommended for addition or removal from list.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
